"Stanley  Myrick" <ancientlore@earthlink.net> writes:
>
> The spoiler said that it takes 70 on the marker to write a Fo Death
> Spellbook. That is why I am in trouble. I have no wishes and one Magic
> Marker at 1:50.

No, 70 is the maximum.  The actual marker charge needed will be a
random amount from half the maximum to one less, so 35-69.  If it
falls in the range 35-50 (roughly 45% chance), you'll write it
successfully.  If not, you'll use up your marker totally.  So, are you
feeling lucky?

An alternative is to write nothing now, and ascend to DL 1 in the
hopes you won't meet Rodney in person again.  If you're lucky, Rodney
may summon nasties including a cockatrice (or you may stumble across a
randomly generated one) before he appears in person, and you can stone
him when he does show up.  Also, it only takes one turn to write a
spellbook once you have the materials ready, so you may want to wait
until he actually shows up before deciding how to handle him.

You still have a wand of death, so you can use that first.  You
probably know this already, but try to put yourself in a position
where you, Rodney, and a wall line up in a horizontal or vertical
line.  If it misses him, you may get him on the reflection from the
wall; if you have reflection too---and you really ought to---it can
bounce again, and you may get three chances to hit him.  This probably
requires you, Rodney, and the wall to be adjacent with no intervening
space, but since Rodney will re-teleport next to you now and then,
getting yourself close to a wall when he appears, if you have time,
may give you this opportunity after a few turns.

Then, when you use up your wand of death, you can reassess whether
trying to write the finger of death spellbook is worth it.

When you get to DL1, you can also consider reverse genociding
cockatrices for corpses and the guaranteed encounter with Rodney.

